<title>USA: Electronic Systems sets stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Electronic Systems sets stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>KENNEWICK, Wash. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronic Systems Technology Inc, a maker of wireless communications hardware, on Wednesday set a stock repurchase plan to acquire up to $100,000 worth of the company's common in open market purchases from brokers and dealers.</p>
<p>The maximum number of shares the company will repurchase from any single shareholder during the duration of the stock repurchase plan will be 10,000 shares.</p>
<p>Electronic Systems shares last closed on December 16 at a price of 1/4 per share.</p>
</text>
